      "problem": "Simplify the expression $\\left| - \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|.$",
      "worked_solution": "Firstly, since $|{-a}| = |a|,$ we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n\\left| \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|.\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication and division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}| & = \\\\ \\frac{|{x}^{2}|}{|10|} & = \\\\ \\frac{|{x}^{2}|}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x^2 \\geq 0$ for any real $x,$ we have that $\\left|x^2\\right|=x^2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{|{x}^{2}|}{10} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
